Data Source & API Management

This is the most critical non-functional requirement for the platform's stability and longevity. The system must be architected as a responsible "good citizen" of the web, robustly handling the unique limitations of each data source.
Requirements:
A centralized request management system must be implemented. This system will be capable of handling configurable delays between requests, retries with exponential backoff for transient errors, and queuing of API calls to respect rate limits.
Each data harvester module (for Google Play, Reddit, etc.) must be independently configurable with its own specific rate limit, delay, and retry settings.
The system must implement comprehensive logging for all API calls and scraping activities, capturing both successful requests and errors to facilitate debugging.
Key Artifact: Data Source Management Matrix: This matrix serves as the single source of truth for the operational constraints of every data source used by Aura. It codifies the findings from the research phase and provides a critical reference for the development team, ensuring that architectural decisions are made with a full understanding of each source's limitations. This prevents costly mistakes, such as treating an unstable scraper with the same confidence as an official API, or building an inefficient workflow that rapidly exhausts a free API quota.
