Performance, Caching, and Scalability

Performance: The perceived performance and responsiveness of the application are paramount to user satisfaction. Given that data collection and analysis can be time-consuming, aggressive caching is not an optional optimization but a core architectural requirement. The heavy and judicious use of Streamlit's caching decorators, specifically @st.cache_data for data-producing functions and @st.cache_resource for loading large, static assets like the sentiment model, is mandatory.17
Scalability: The MVP is intentionally designed for a single-user, on-demand execution model. The choice of SQLite as the data persistence layer is a deliberate trade-off, prioritizing simplicity and zero-configuration setup over concurrent-user scalability. The PRD acknowledges that should the application evolve into a multi-user platform with features like scheduled analyses or persistent user accounts, the data persistence layer will represent a primary scaling bottleneck and will need to be migrated to a more robust client-server database system, such as PostgreSQL.

Legal and Ethical Considerations

The operation of the Aura platform must adhere to strict legal and ethical standards to ensure its long-term viability and responsible conduct.
Terms of Service Compliance: The application will strictly adhere to the published Terms of Service for all official APIs it consumes, including those from Google (for YouTube) and Reddit.
Responsible Scraping: For tools that rely on web scraping (google-play-scraper, app-store-web-scraper, instaloader), the application will be configured to maintain a responsible request rate to avoid placing undue load on the target services. Where applicable, it will respect the directives found in the robots.txt files of the target domains.
Data Privacy: The application will only process data that is explicitly public. No attempts will be made to access private user information, circumvent login walls, or otherwise retrieve data not intended for public consumption. All analysis will be performed on aggregated, anonymized data wherever possible.